  <ym-title|Graded quotient estimate><label|graded-quotient-estimate>

  Read Scott J-section.tex:17\U138, especially lem:J-signed-local and
  lem:J-graded-quotient. The new fragment proves the graded distance
  implication from the already stated triangular coefficient transfer, graph
  remainder bounds, local trial comparison and normalized-null physical
  representative lemma. It carefully identifies the transported microscopic
  low plane with lower physical fields through ALL spectator tests; it does
  not replace corrected inclusions with raw polynomial inclusions.

  The common stage conditions give both the low cone and the high-degree
  step, and the product of column constants has subpower growth. The low-cone
  error uses \|x_fine\|\<leqslant\>Y as well as \|d x_fine\|\<leqslant\>2Y;
  retaining this distinction makes the stated absorption factor valid. Output
  constants do not depend on the chosen ordered coefficient refinement.

  This closes the abstract graded quotient implication conditional on the
  same upstream marked/null interfaces already retained by Chapter13. The
  all-marker cluster grouping/extraction and phase-uniform signed residual
  are still separate obligations. Independent review pending.
